#!/usr/bin/env python3
# Some portions generated by Codex.
import pathlib,json
p=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent;s=json.loads((p/'summary.json').read_text());ids=json.loads((p/'source-identities.json').read_text())
a=['# Read-resource holder: actual Workbench results','','## Verdict','','The new read-resource holder did not demonstrate an incremental HTTP latency or throughput benefit on depth. Pooled completion times were effectively identical; the four paired blocks were variable. Neither the resource-only arm nor the factorial interaction establishes a win. Do not promote this candidate on performance grounds from this experiment.','','The workload is real on-disk LMDB with synthetic RDF data, actual RDF4J Server binary output, actual Workbench Java decoding and NDJSON serialization, and a Node streaming client. It excludes browser rendering, concurrent QPS, remote-network effects and the historical wide eight-million-row fixture.','','## Immutable arms','']
for x in ids:a.append(f'- **{x}**: `{ids[x]}`.')
a+=['','All arms use the same reconstructed frozen server/dependency stack, pinned PR #6440 writer, compact identity mapping, memo/IR flags and full six-slot 100,000-row response. The holder layer contains only 105 LmdbSailStore family classes. Its pre-edit 104-class family was byte-identical to incumbent. Cancellation changes, initializer null-slot restoration and the grouped test-only observer are excluded. The archive branch is not a runtime identity.','','## Protocol and qualification','','One prespecified four-block Latin square, four independent fresh JVMs per arm. Each fork completed 60 warmups and 30 measured sequential queries: 1,440 requests total, 480 measured. Every request passed compiled IR, memo, binary MIME, row count, no-spill, ledger cleanup and class-origin checks. Four separate untimed qualification queries validated every term, uniqueness and dual checksums. All samples were retained; no trimming or additional clean round. Startup and client setup are outside POST-to-EOF latency.','','Correctness: eight focused tests and 110 integration tests passed separately on resource-only and combined, with three expected gated skips in each integration selection. The three corrected gated fixtures then passed separately on both arms using a test-only observer that is absent from timed classpaths. This is scoped validation, not a whole-repository pass.','','## Clean means','','| Arm | EOF ms | First row ms | Derived rows/s | Fork EOF range ms |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for x in ids:
 v=s['arms'][x];m=v['means'];lo,hi=v['forkRangeEofMs'];a.append(f"| {x} | {m['eofMs']:.3f} | {m['firstRowMs']:.3f} | {100000000/m['eofMs']:.0f} | {lo:.3f}–{hi:.3f} |")
a+=['','Rows/s is the reciprocal of sequential full-response latency, not concurrent serving capacity.','','| Contrast | EOF reduction % | Paired reductions % | Descriptive 95% interval % |','|---|---:|---|---|']
for k,v in s['contrasts'].items():
 q=v['eofMs'];a.append(f"| {k} | {q['latencyReductionPercent']:.3f} | {', '.join(f'{z:+.2f}' for z in q['pairedReductionPercent'])} | {q['descriptive95ReductionInterval'][0]:+.2f} to {q['descriptive95ReductionInterval'][1]:+.2f} |")
v=s['interaction']['eofMs'];a += ['',f"Factorial geometric interaction ratio: **{v['geometricInteractionRatio']:.3f}**, descriptive 95% interval **{v['descriptive95RatioInterval'][0]:.3f}–{v['descriptive95RatioInterval'][1]:.3f}**. Values below one suggest supermultiplicative latency reduction, but this wide interval crosses one. Intervals use paired log fork means and t with three degrees of freedom; they are unadjusted for multiple contrasts and do not establish equivalence.",'','## All independent fork means','','| Fork | Arm | EOF ms | First row ms |','|---|---|---:|---:|']
for f in s['forks']:a.append(f"| {f['name']} | {f['arm']} | {f['means']['eofMs']:.3f} | {f['means']['firstRowMs']:.3f} |")
a+=['','## Convergence and limitations','','| Arm | First measured third ms | Middle third ms | Last third ms |','|---|---:|---:|---:|']
for x,v in s['arms'].items():a.append('| '+x+' | '+' | '.join(f'{z:.3f}' for z in v['measuredThirdMeanEofMs'])+' |')
a+=['','Longer fixed warmup did not prove convergence: the combined arm still decreases across measured thirds. We retain the full prespecified interval rather than select its faster tail. Four forks per arm constrain precision; request samples within a fork are not independent replications. Earlier embedded depth gains do not establish a gain through this HTTP pipeline.','','Whole-JVM GC logs include startup/warmup, not query-attributed pauses. Heap-used before/after snapshots are not allocation or retained heap. RSS was not collected; no memory-capacity conclusion follows. The browser remains unmeasured following the prior policy-blocked launch; no retry or bypass occurred.','','## Evidence','','`summary.json` retains every fork and index, GC summaries, first application-query values and all contrasts. `runs/matched-*` retain raw request metrics, commands and logs. `protocol.json`, source IDs, class manifests and the frozen common manifests establish provenance. Setup correction is recorded in `SETUP-NOTES.md`; it occurred before any comparison. Separate JFR results will be added in `HTTP-PROFILES.md`, never pooled into the clean timing population.','']
(p/'RESULTS.md').write_text('\n'.join(a))

with (p/"RESULTS.md").open("a") as f: f.write('\n### Published raw-evidence packaging\n\n`evidence/index.json` and its ordered `poolChunks` losslessly reconstruct all 3,684 textual run files. Concatenate indexed UTF-8 pool lines for ordinary files. For `compactJsonFrom` log entries, compact the referenced reconstructed JSON by removing whitespace only outside strings, then append a newline. Verify every recorded SHA-256. `package-evidence.py` verified exact byte round-trips for all 32,022,432 original bytes; originals remain local. Raw JFR and multi-gigabyte full-stack exports are excluded; compact full-stack analysis summaries are published separately.\n')
